  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pakistan Humanitarian Empowerment Program (PHEP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the successful interventions from the previous Pakistan flood response&#x2014;such as cash-for-health initiatives, rehabilitation of basic health units, and Livelihoods and Household (LLH) support&#x2014;this program aims to deliver targeted assistance in one to two geographical areas in Pakistan.
The program seeks to enhance the resilience, health, and socio-economic capacity of Afghan migrants, internally displaced persons (IDPs), and host communities across four districts in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa (KP) and Balochistan. This will be achieved through integrated, equitable, and sustainable interventions in:

Health
Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH)
Livelihoods
National Society Development (NSD)

These efforts aim to improve health outcomes and strengthen livelihoods through the provision of transferable vocational skills. The program is designed to address immediate humanitarian needs while laying a strong foundation for long-term recovery and resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
